% M7-T22 / D-0086 (c): the bench/fuzz sweep's CRASH, exit 2, `Alldiff: ladder rung has no
% constraint id` (`bench/fuzz/gen.py ad 25203`, shrunk greedily; ad 25705 and others are
% the same shape). FIXED; an ordinary passing model test whose proof is verified on every
% run.
%
% THE DEFECT. Not a View, and not a ladder element failed to materialise: the rung asked
% for does not exist in any encoding. Element shaves x6's upper bound to 3 at the root
% (declared 1..4), and a Hall interval [a, 4] then pushes x6 out of it. Stage 1's
% [overshoot_cancel] cancels the residue y_ge_(b+1) by the ladder rungs from hi(y)+1 to b
% -- but with b = decl_hi(x6) = 4 the residue x6_ge_5 is the constant false, and the rung
% x6_ge_5 -> x6_ge_4 it asked for is not a row of the model. Its guard did not state the
% condition its own comment gives (b + 1 <= decl_hi(y)).
%
% THE FIX is that condition in [overshoot_cancel]'s guard. Break: the pre-fix binary
% (sha256 a57f2961...) exits 2.
var 1..1: x0 :: output_var;
var 1..1: x1 :: output_var;
var 3..4: x2 :: output_var;
var 1..4: x3 :: output_var;
var 1..1: x4 :: output_var;
var 2..2: x5 :: output_var;
var 1..4: x6 :: output_var;
constraint all_different_int([x6,x2,x3,x5]);
constraint array_int_element(x6,[1,4,2,2],x5);
constraint array_int_element(x3,[1,3,1,3],x6);
solve :: int_search([x1,x6,x2,x4,x0,x3,x5], smallest, indomain_split, complete) satisfy;
